Dis</source><year>2001</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>S166</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kemp</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Boxshall</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Nhlema</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Salaniponi</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Squire</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Application of a geographical information system to assess the relationship between socioeconomic status and access for TB care in urban Lilongwe</article-title><source>Int J Tuberc Lung Dis</source><year>2001</year><fpage>5</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Luhanga</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Chilimampunga</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Salaniponi</surname><given-names>FML</given-names></name><name><surname>Squire</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Kemp</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Gender differences in access to treatment and caring for TB patients within the households</article-title><source>Int J Tuberc Lung Dis</source><year>2001</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>S167</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kemp</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Mann</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Nhlema Simwaka</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Salaniponi</surname><given-names>FML</given-names></name><name><surname>Squire</surname><given-names>SB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Can Malawi's poor afford free TB services? Patients and household costs associate